    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 1248 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> in 1269, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> rule in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maghreb">Maghreb</a>; in 1276 they founded Fes Jdid as their administrative and military centre.</li><li>Abu al-Hasan (r. 1331–1348) conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> in 1337 and defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsids</a> in 1347, making himself master of a territory from southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> to Tripoli, but lost his eastern lands within a year.</li><li>A Portuguese–Castilian army defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty">Marinids</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado">Battle of Río Salado</a> in 1340 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeciras">Algeciras</a> in 1344, expelling them from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a> for good.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Abu al-Hasan copied the Qur'an in his own hand four times, sending copies to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aqsa-mosque">Al-Aqsa Mosque</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>; a fifth, begun at Bijaya for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebron">Hebron</a>, was finished by his son after his dethronement.</p></aside>
    </section>

